# /ctcp and /ctcpreply (`IRCClient.m:3227-3262`): the command uppercased,
# PING with the time as Textual's `sendCTCPPing:` writes it.
! welcome
! type console /ctcp bob version
> PRIVMSG bob VERSION
! type console /ctcp bob ping
> PRIVMSG bob :PING 1800000000.000000
! type console /ctcp bob clientinfo extra words
> PRIVMSG bob :CLIENTINFO extra words
! type console /ctcpreply bob version Textual GTK
> NOTICE bob :VERSION Textual GTK
! type console /ctcp bob
? line console Invalid syntax: “CTCP <nickname> <command> [extra]“
? notice Invalid syntax: “CTCP <nickname> <command> [extra]“
? registered textual
